ding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">47:58</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">In Our Time</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Ancient Egypt had no queens: she could only be king, and was erased 20 years after her death</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Hatshepsut took power gradually from the position of regent, building royal authority through temples, trade and oracles; about 20 years after her death Thutmose III erased her on a large scale.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ancient Egypt</span><span class=\"tag\">Hatshepsut</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The real fix for alignment: humans have to keep faith with models first Bostrom&#x27;s core judgment: capability lockdown was never more than a temporary measure, and the real fix is alignment — which may require humans to start keeping their word to models now, because for a misaligned AI facing deletion, betting on a 5% chance of seizing power is the rational move. Odd Lots Odd Lots Nick Bostrom on What Happens if AI Solves All of Our Problems AI alignment Reward hacking Reinforcement learning Digital mind ethics Automation and distribution Longevity post-instrumental condition sandbagging reward hacking Goodharting moral patienthood simulation hypothesis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-oddlots-把-ai-關進盒子只是權宜-真解法是人先變得可信/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">55:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The real fix for alignment: humans have to keep faith with models first</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Bostrom&#x27;s core judgment: capability lockdown was never more than a temporary measure, and the real fix is alignment — which may require humans to start keeping their word to models now, because for a misaligned AI facing deletion, betting on a 5% chance of seizing power is the rational move.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI alignment</span><span class=\"tag\">Reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"The Korean Wave isn&#x27;t a cultural miracle — it&#x27;s a government-planned industrial counterattack From the rubble of the Korean War to BTS and Parasite, the Korean Wave looks like a cultural phenomenon. It is actually the route two generations of leaders, from Park Chung-hee to Kim Dae-jung, took to turn culture into an export industry using the instruments of the state. Throughline Throughline How Korean culture went global Korean Wave K-pop Industrial policy Cultural export Korean history Globalization Korean Wave Chaebol 3S policy Entrepreneurial state National humiliation Day\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-throughline-韓流不是文化奇蹟-是政府策劃的產業反攻/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2984x2984+0+0/resize/3000/quality/66/format/jpg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F48%2Fce%2Fb906c9c74361bf187754f9d6695e%2Fb1747544-3d16-4a7f-b5c6-28ab69610ca0.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">48:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Throughline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The Korean Wave isn&#x27;t a cultural miracle — it&#x27;s a government-planned industrial counterattack</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">From the rubble of the Korean War to BTS and Parasite, the Korean Wave looks like a cultural phenomenon. It is actually the route two generations of leaders, from Park Chung-hee to Kim Dae-jung, took to turn culture into an export industry using the instruments of the state.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Korean Wave</span><span class=\"tag\">K-pop</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Banks Reconcile by Phone, Not by System: One Wrong Ticket Can Cost Hundreds of Millions Who owes whom, and how much, between two institutions is often settled not by an automated reconciliation system but by phone calls, personal relationships, and the unspoken understanding that ‘we still have to do business together tomorrow’. Complex Systems Complex Systems Two banks can&#x27;t agree on fourth-grade math | Alex Elliott Clearing &amp; settlement Middle &amp; back office Prime brokerage Trading incidents Risk management Order flow MPID (Market Participant Identifier) Reg NMS / NBBO (national best bid and offer) Prime broker Golden record Payment for order flow Busting a trade\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-complexsys-兩家銀行連四年級數學都對不齊/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/St-giYMCNRxOqSi0db5uiFmB2vKoxHbZlWUVWcLx51E/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS82OWRl/MDRmYjU0Mjk5MjNj/Yzk1OTE5MTQ2ZGJl/NjUxZi5wbmc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:03:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Complex Systems</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Banks Reconcile by Phone, Not by System: One Wrong Ticket Can Cost Hundreds of Millions</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Who owes whom, and how much, between two institutions is often settled not by an automated reconciliation system but by phone calls, personal relationships, and the unspoken understanding that ‘we still have to do business together tomorrow’.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Clearing &amp; settlement</span><span class=\"tag\">Middle &amp; back office</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"The Maya ballgame was ritual, not sport: the sacrificed-winner story is invented The Mesoamerican ballgame is humanity&#x27;s earliest rubber-ball team sport, but it was religious ritual first: the court re-staged the creation myth, and the people who could be killed were captives who lost a ritual re-enactment. The idea that the winners were sacrificed was made up later. The Ancients The Ancients The Maya Ballgame Maya civilization Mesoamerica Ballgame Religious ritual Archaeology Sports history Popol Vuh Mesoamerica Hero Twins yoke morning glory ball court\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-ancients-瑪雅球賽首先是宗教-贏家被獻祭是謊言/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/6215f9e74b795a6299fd3b58/1786978898442-91a04567-af46-4b5d-9e78-085d63eb48cf.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Ancients</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The Maya ballgame was ritual, not sport: the sacrificed-winner story is invented</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Mesoamerican ballgame is humanity&#x27;s earliest rubber-ball team sport, but it was religious ritual first: the court re-staged the creation myth, and the people who could be killed were captives who lost a ritual re-enactment. The idea that the winners were sacrificed was made up later.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Maya civilization</span><span class=\"tag\">Mesoamerica</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Burning tokens to stack up agents is a transitional strategy, not the endgame Silicon Valley is shifting from mindless token burning to careful accounting: a local open-source model can do real work on a dollar a day of electricity, yet when a genuinely hard problem shows up, a smarter model can still nail in one shot the answer a billion-token group chat could not argue its way to. Saving money and top-tier intelligence are not in conflict. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E249｜Token經濟轉點：OpenClaw、Hermes到本地自研的Agent進化之路 Token Economics Agent Engineering Open-Source Models Local Deployment B2B Startups Infrastructure Investing OpenClaw Agentic Loop FDE (Forward Deployed Engineer) Agent Native Jevons Paradox Gödel machine\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-sv101-堆agent燒token是過渡策略-不是終局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/f/f0f20376-8faf-4940-b920-84af6c734e2d/cover.jpg?v=6\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">1:27:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Burning tokens to stack up agents is a transitional strategy, not the endgame</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Silicon Valley is shifting from mindless token burning to careful accounting: a local open-source model can do real work on a dollar a day of electricity, yet when a genuinely hard problem shows up, a smarter model can still nail in one shot the answer a billion-token group chat could not argue its way to. Saving money and top-tier intelligence are not in conflict.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Token Economics</span><span class=\"tag\">Agent Engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Thirty Thousand Canadians Moved: The Young Were Saved, the Old Lost Everything From 1954, nearly thirty thousand people in Newfoundland, Canada, were moved from remote fishing villages to towns. The younger generation gained education and a way out; the old and the Inuit lost their homes, scattered until there was no way left to reach one another. Resettlement has no single verdict. Witness History Witness History Canada&#x27;s controversial resettlement programme Urbanization Resettlement Newfoundland Oral history Regional policy Community collapse outport growth centre Confederation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-19-witness-加拿大三萬人大搬遷-最好的事與最糟的事/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/400x400/p0kt82ds.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">9:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Witness History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0819</span></div>\n<h2>Thirty Thousand Canadians Moved: The Young Were Saved, the Old Lost Everything</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">From 1954, nearly thirty thousand people in Newfoundland, Canada, were moved from remote fishing villages to towns. The younger generation gained education and a way out; the old and the Inuit lost their homes, scattered until there was no way left to reach one another. Resettlement has no single verdict.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Urbanization</span><span class=\"tag\">Resettlement</span>\n</div></div></a>"]